# In an array of doubles a NaN marks a hole, so a number is stored raw only after it has passed `x === x`. A number that fails the test goes to the stub.
# The emitter used to check two raw stores of the library's own operations for that, and none of the program's: a store by key, a push and an append.
# With the switches that make the emitters check proofs, each of them is checked now. In a user's build, nothing is added.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeNoNaNStores: the test of each of these paths is omitted. In a default build the element, which is 0 / 0, would silently disappear.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.fails = "all";
# RIGHT: true 0.5,NaN,0.5
# RIGHT-NEXT: true 1.5,0.5,NaN,0.5
# RIGHT-NEXT: true 1.5,0.5,NaN,0.5
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime globalThis.fails = "all";
# HELD: true 0.5,NaN,0.5
# HELD-NEXT: true 1.5,0.5,NaN,0.5
# HELD-NEXT: true 1.5,0.5,NaN,0.5
# HELD-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(PASSES): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,AssumeNoNaNStores
# PASSES: true 0.5,0.5,0.5
# PASSES-NEXT: true 1.5,0.5,0.5,0.5
# PASSES-NEXT: true 1.5,0.5,0.5,0.5
# PASSES-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(SILENT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=AssumeNoNaNStores globalThis.fails = "all";
# SILENT: false 0.5,,0.5
# SILENT-NEXT: false 1.5,0.5,,0.5
# SILENT-NEXT: true 1.5,0.5,,0.5
# RUN(STORE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,AssumeNoNaNStores globalThis.fails = "store";
# STORE: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# STORE-NEXT: found an unexpected value in the result of an operation
# STORE: crashed with
# RUN(PUSH): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,AssumeNoNaNStores globalThis.fails = "push";
# PUSH: true 0.5,0.5,0.5
# PUSH: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# PUSH-NEXT: found an unexpected value in the result of an operation
# PUSH: crashed with
# RUN(APPEND): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,AssumeNoNaNStores globalThis.fails = "append";
# APPEND: true 1.5,0.5,0.5,0.5
# APPEND: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# APPEND-NEXT: found an unexpected value in the result of an operation
# APPEND: crashed with
